      {
        "id": 80872,
        "name": "Koga",
        "username": "Koga",
        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/koga/{size}/2058_2.png",
        "created_at": "2013-11-07T21:18:50.000Z",
        "cooked": "<aside class=\"quote group-playtesters\" data-username=\"Foote\">\n<div class=\"title\">\n<div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n<img loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/foote/48/1877_2.png\" class=\"avatar\"> Foote:</div>\n<blockquote>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<div><b>Envisioner wrote:</b><br><blockquote>Does that mean it's Drupal's fault that my outdated browser continually crashes this site?&nbsp; Do you suppose that if I contacted them about it, they'd have anything to say besides telling me, just like everything else, that I am expected to update my browser whether I like it or not?&nbsp; Probably not, I suspect, and therefore I won't likely bother trying.\n&nbsp;\n</blockquote></div>\nChrome. Why you would use any other browser is besides me.\n</blockquote>\n</aside>\n<p>A friend of mine once tried Chrome, it rewrote his security settings that he had spent a long time customizing, so he promptly uninstalled it.</p>",
